hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1306","It is narrated by Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “The Prophet forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, from buying and selling, from seeking lost things, from appealing to poetry, and from setting out to speak on Friday before... “Prayer” means in the mosque"
